  },
  "content": {
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "order": 1,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s1",
            "text": "Competitive eating—or speed eating—is exactly what its name suggests."
          },
          {
            "id": "s2",
            "text": "Contestants 1 eat as much as they can, usually within a time limit."
          },
          {
            "id": "s3",
            "text": "Eating competitions can involve various foods—pizza, pies, ice cream, chili peppers."
          },
          {
            "id": "s4",
            "text": "They can also offer large prizes to the winners."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "order": 2,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s5",
            "text": "The world’s largest competitive eating event is Nathan’s Famous Hot Dog Eating Contest."
          },
          {
            "id": "s6",
            "text": "The event is held every Fourth of July in Brooklyn, New York."
          },
          {
            "id": "s7",
            "text": "According to legend, 2 this tradition began over a hundred years ago."
          },
          {
            "id": "s8",
            "text": "Four immigrants 3 were arguing about who loved their new country the most."
          },
          {
            "id": "s9",
            "text": "Finally, they worked out a way to decide."
          },
          {
            "id": "s10",
            "text": "They would see who could eat the most of a famous American food—the hot dog."
          },
          {
            "id": "s11",
            "text": "James Mullen, an Irish immigrant, won by eating 13 hot dogs in 12 minutes."
          },
          {
            "id": "s12",
            "text": "Nathan’s Fourth of July tradition was born."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "order": 3,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s13",
            "text": "The current champion * of the contest is Joey Chestnut."
          },
          {
            "id": "s14",
            "text": "Chestnut—an American—also holds the world record for hot dog eating—74 in less than 10 minutes."
          },
          {
            "id": "s15",
            "text": "That’s just over 8 seconds per hot dog."
          },
          {
            "id": "s16",
            "text": "For many years, the Nathan’s Contest champion was Takeru Kobayashi from Japan."
          },
          {
            "id": "s17",
            "text": "He is smaller and lighter than Chestnut, and doesn’t look like an eating champion."
          },
          {
            "id": "s18",
            "text": "However, he holds many world records for eating different types of food."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "order": 4,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s19",
            "text": "Not everybody thinks competitive eating is a good thing."
          },
          {
            "id": "s20",
            "text": "It can be unhealthy for the contestants, and many people in the world are going hungry."
          },
          {
            "id": "s21",
            "text": "Kobayashi first won the event in 2001 when he was 23 years old."
          },
          {
            "id": "s22",
            "text": "So are eating competitions in bad taste?"
          },
          {
            "id": "s23",
            "text": "For competitive eaters, it’s a sport like any other."
          },
          {
            "id": "s24",
            "text": "As Kobayashi says, “Food fighters … think of themselves as athletes.”"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "analysis": {
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "topic": {
          "label": "定义与概述"
        },
        "main_idea": {
          "text": "竞技进食（速度进食）是指在限定时间内尽可能多吃各种食物，并可能获得丰厚奖品的比赛。"
        },
        "key_details": [
          {
            "source_ids": [
              "s2"
            ],
            "meaning": "参赛者通常在时间限制内吃下最多的食物。"
          },
          {
            "source_ids": [
              "s3"
            ],
            "meaning": "比赛食物种类多样，包括披萨、派、冰淇淋和辣椒等。"
          },
          {
            "source_ids": [
              "s4"
            ],
            "meaning": "获胜者可以获得大额奖金。"
          }
        ],
        "function": {
          "type": "introduction"
        },
        "relation_to_previous": null,
        "signals": [
          {
            "text": "Competitive eating—or speed eating—is exactly what its name suggests.",
            "source_id": "s1",
            "role": "topic_sentence"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "topic": {
          "label": "起源传说"
        },
        "main_idea": {
          "text": "世界上最大的竞技进食活动是纳森热狗大赛，其起源与一百多年前四位移民争论谁更爱美国有关。"
        },
        "key_details": [
          {
            "source_ids": [
              "s5",
              "s6"
            ],
            "meaning": "该赛事每年7月4日在纽约布鲁克林举行。"
          },
          {
            "source_ids": [
              "s8",
              "s10"
            ],
            "meaning": "四位移民通过比赛吃热狗的数量来决定谁更爱国。"
          },
          {
            "source_ids": [
              "s11"
            ],
            "meaning": "爱尔兰移民詹姆斯·穆伦在12分钟内吃了13个热狗获胜。"
          }
        ],
        "function": {
          "type": "background"
        },
        "relation_to_previous": {
          "type": "example",
          "target": "p1"
        },
        "signals": [
          {
